The VGA core takes a `vram` region its owner backed already (2ksbox,
M15, ADR-018, 2026-09-22).

`vga_common_init` allocates `vga.vram` itself, unconditionally. The
`d3dpt-vga` adapter now backs it first when its Direct3D executor runs
in another process (Wine on the host, on a Linux or macOS host below
DXVK's Vulkan 1.3 floor): a region of that executor's shared file
through `memory_region_init_ram_from_fd`, so the guest's VRAM and
command window are the bytes the other process maps, and a batch runs
where the guest wrote it. The core skips its own allocation when the
region already has a size, and refuses one of the wrong size; every
other VGA is unchanged.

diff --git a/hw/display/vga.c b/hw/display/vga.c
index 9bc496c8ee..0251043571 100644
--- a/hw/display/vga.c
+++ b/hw/display/vga.c
@@ -2260,11 +2260,25 @@ bool vga_common_init(VGACommonState *s, Object *obj, Error **errp)
         return false;
     }
 
-    memory_region_init_ram_flags_nomigrate(&s->vram, obj, "vga.vram",
-                                           s->vram_size, 0, &local_err);
-    if (local_err) {
-        error_propagate(errp, local_err);
-        return false;
+    /*
+     * 2ksbox: the owner may have backed the region already -- d3dpt-vga
+     * does, with a region of the shared file its out-of-process Direct3D
+     * executor reads VRAM from (memory_region_init_ram_from_fd) -- and
+     * then it is taken as it is; a region of size 0 is one nobody made.
+     */
+    if (memory_region_size(&s->vram)) {
+        if (memory_region_size(&s->vram) != s->vram_size) {
+            error_setg(errp, "vga.vram was backed with %" PRIu64 " bytes, not %u",
+                       memory_region_size(&s->vram), s->vram_size);
+            return false;
+        }
+    } else {
+        memory_region_init_ram_flags_nomigrate(&s->vram, obj, "vga.vram",
+                                               s->vram_size, 0, &local_err);
+        if (local_err) {
+            error_propagate(errp, local_err);
+            return false;
+        }
     }
     vmstate_register_ram(&s->vram, s->global_vmstate ? NULL : DEVICE(obj));
     xen_register_framebuffer(&s->vram);
